  "variation": {
    "seeded": true,
    "notes": "Wave width and height, the bumps along the crest, spray and the puddle shape vary per cast. The 760 ms roll and the crash moment stay fixed so the hit always lands on the same frame."
  },
  "director_notes": "Heavy area spell built around a new `wave` layer: a curling wall that rises out of a pool at the caster's feet, rolls about 3.5 units and collapses over the target. Choices: (1) a 420 ms swell with ground rumble so the player sees it coming; (2) the wall grows as it travels and the lip curls further until it throws over, so it reads as a breaking wave rather than a sliding block; (3) the crash is a tall crown plus a forward-flung sheet and a foam cloud, then a wide puddle that outlasts the spell. Hero view 3/4; side shows the profile best. Water stays mid-blue with white only in the foam so it reads on any background."
}
